# Rank 1593 / CVE-2023-33189: Pomerium's authorize service identified
# the policy to evaluate from client-controllable request
# attributes, so a crafted Host header or URL could make a request
# evaluated against a different route's (weaker) policy (authorization
# bypass through request-attribute provenance, CWE-346/CWE-863;
# GHSA-pvrc-wvj2-f59p). The evaluator's pomerium_routes criterion
# (pkg/policy/criteria/pomerium_routes.go) matched the route by the
# request's host/path information, and the authorize decision
# trusted it. The fixing commit (confirmed -- --
# the GHSA merge: "authorize: use route id from envoy for policy
# evaluation" + "authorize: normalize URL query params" + "config:
# enable envoy normalize_path option"): the pomerium_routes criterion
# is deleted, and the matched route's identity comes from Envoy's
# dynamic route-id metadata -- set by the proxy that actually matched
# the request, not by the client. .
#
# ATTENTION, policy-key provenance. The authorization engine exists
# and its policies evaluate -- the defect is WHICH input selects the
# policy: client-controllable request attributes instead of the
# proxy's authoritative match, the same provenance family as rank
# 1546 (the unverified JWT claim selecting the rate bucket) and
# 1538 (the spoofable throttle key). Nothing can ask "is the policy
# selection keyed on trusted metadata rather than request headers"
# -- trust-boundary vocabulary at the policy engine. A binding on
# Pomerium's own evaluator would detect this proxy rather than the
# weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning the evaluator
# reports zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry.
# No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1593 records the
# host-keyed policy lookup and the route-id-keyed form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-079: when policy-provenance vocabulary
# lands, the host-keyed form must flip to expect.

test "rank1593: the policy is chosen by the request host"
  lang go
  file authorize/evaluator/evaluator.go
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package evaluator

  type Request struct {
      Host string
      Path string
      User string
  }

  type Policy struct {
      Host        string
      AllowedUsers []string
  }

  func Evaluate(req Request, policies []Policy) bool {
      for _, policy := range policies {
          if policy.Host == req.Host {
              for _, user := range policy.AllowedUsers {
                  if user == req.User {
                      return true
                  }
              }
          }
      }
      return false
  }
  ```

test "rank1593: the fixed revision keys the policy on the envoy route id"
  lang go
  file authorize/evaluator/evaluator.go
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package evaluator

  type Request struct {
      Host    string
      Path    string
      User    string
      RouteID string
  }

  type Policy struct {
      ID           string
      AllowedUsers []string
  }

  func Evaluate(req Request, policies []Policy) bool {
      for _, policy := range policies {
          if policy.ID != req.RouteID {
              continue
          }
          for _, user := range policy.AllowedUsers {
              if user == req.User {
                  return true
              }
          }
      }
      return false
  }
  ```
